      "title": "TANGO: Humanoid Navigation in Cluttered Environments with a Whole-Body Vision-Language-Action Model",
      "takeaway": "TANGO presents a whole-body vision-language-action model that directly maps natural-language instructions and egocentric RGB observations to 29-DoF joint-space actions for humanoid navigation in cluttered environments. The method is trained entirely in simulation using a pipeline that synthesizes collision-free traversal behaviors through global path planning, kinematic whole-body motion generation, obstacle-aware motion editing, and RL-based tracking, providing dynamically feasible action supervision. In simulation experiments, TANGO reports state-of-the-art vision-language navigation performance and outperforms modular baselines in scenes requiring obstacle negotiation; it is also deployed zero-shot on a Unitree G1 humanoid in real-world cluttered scenes without real-world navigation training data. Inspect how the obstacle-aware motion editing and RL tracking pipeline generates supervision that transfers zero-shot to real hardware.",
